***************************** T A L Y S **************************2825 1451  186
                                                                  2825 1451  187
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   2825 1451  188
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      2825 1451  189
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    2825 1451  190
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     2825 1451  191
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  2825 1451  192
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        2825 1451  193
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    2825 1451  194
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         2825 1451  195
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      2825 1451  196
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    2825 1451  197
stored in this data file:                                         2825 1451  198
                                                                  2825 1451  199
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   2825 1451  200
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     2825 1451  201
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 2825 1451  202
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   2825 1451  203
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                2825 1451  204
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   2825 1451  205
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    2825 1451  206
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        2825 1451  207
- Recoil data                                                     2825 1451  208
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           2825 1451  209
- Total particle energy spectra                                   2825 1451  210
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      2825 1451  211
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        2825 1451  212
- Residual production cross sections                              2825 1451  213
                                                                  2825 1451  214
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            2825 1451  215
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        2825 1451  216
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   2825 1451  217
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                2825 1451  218
                                                                  2825 1451  219
